<title>BULGARIA: Yield rises to 0.45 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises to 0.45 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield rose further to 0.45 percent on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Friday as the issue was undersubscribed, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity at Thursday's auction was 0.43 percent, up from 0.40 percent on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 10 billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3040497003</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     10 bln levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 30</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 28</p>
<p> Bids received		 9.95 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   99.55 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 9.95 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  99.55 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     0.45 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
